{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["With a rod — with an object that a person is accustomed to strike his slave with to discipline him. But with a sword, by the plain sense, he is liable to death even after a day or two, for this is not a method of discipline but of murder — and this speaks of a Canaanite slave. But a Hebrew slave, an Israelite, is not his property; rather כשכיר כתושב יהיה עמך, and his law is like an Israelite's in all matters — except that his master gives him a Canaanite maidservant."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:42:24.967806386Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}